  "notes": "Guitar-rooted melodic pop-rap migrating to country-pop, which is the lane the entry names, so the straight class wins: `halfTime` false and `backbeat_24` with \"swirling percussion and shaker for the guitar mode\" as the perc lanes and a brushed/live feel in the humanize block. The half-time trap kit the entry also documents is left unencoded rather than blended. The harmony is the strongest researched fact here and it is transcribed as degrees, not qualities: \"Circles runs Cmaj7—Em/B—Fmaj7—Fm then Cmaj7—Em/B—Fmaj7—G6, i.e. Imaj7—iii(inv)—IVmaj7—iv then resolving on V6\", so the families are [\"I\",\"iii\",\"IV\",\"iv\"] and [\"I\",\"iii\",\"IV\",\"V\"] with the major-7th colour living in `extensions` (seventh 0.5 is the highest in this batch, because major-7th is the stated signature). Keys are the entry's own recurrence list. The 808 is authored because the entry names it — \"808 sub with short slides in the rap mode\" — as `counter_riff` so that the pop mode's \"electric bass doubling the guitar root motion\" still generates; that doubling is the high `followRootsProb` on a kick mirror. Melody encodes \"a narrow, laconic mid-baritone band [that] repeats short cells rather than developing long phrases\" as a low register ceiling, `riff_loop`, `twoBarCellRepeat` and a small `motifPitchCount`. Arrangement encodes the documented omission: no prechorus in the higher-weighted structure. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are every drum probability, the humanize block and `bpm.mode` 135 (the research gives 76—160 with cluster 120—150, so the mode is that cluster's midpoint). ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research rates it high-medium and says the rap-mode drum specifics are genre-conventional; the catalogue tempo band carries its [LOW-CONF] mark. ⚠ `tier` is `standard` even though the section orientation lists him among the \"Six flagship names (Swift, Eilish, Rodrigo, Lipa, Post Malone, Grande) … written here as artists in their own right\": docs/dataset-protocol.md requires `confidence: high` for `flagship`, and this entry's own line is \"Confidence: high-medium\", so promoting the tier would mean rating the model above its research. The tier follows the confidence the research states; the orientation line is the half that overstates.",
